WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.334
Manhattan District Attorney Alvin Bragg.

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.535
Let's listen in

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.672
on a New York Supreme Court indictment

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.241
returned by a Manhattan grand jury

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:11.311
on 34 felony counts of falsifying

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.413
business records in the first degree

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.715
under New York state law.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.250
It is a felony

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.319
to falsify business records

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.855
with intent to defraud an intent

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.991
to conceal another crime.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.694
That is exactly what this case is about.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.531
34 false statements

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.234
made to cover up other crimes.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.336
These are felony crimes

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.771
in New York State,

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.874
no matter who you are,

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.977
we cannot and will not normalize

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.680
serious criminal conduct.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.716
The defendant repeatedly made

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.451
false statements

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.553
on New York business records.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.355
He also caused others

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:58.224
to make false statements

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.159
The defendant claimed

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.027
that he was paying Michael Cohen

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:04.497
for legal services performed in 2017.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.700
This simply was not true.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.603
And it was a false statement

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.872
that the defendant made month

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.041
after month in 2017

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:19.179
April May, June

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.981
and so on through the rest of the year.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:26.052
For nine straight months,

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.254
the defendant held documents in his hand

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.990
containing this key lie

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.860
that he was paying Michael Cohen

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.297
for legal services performed in 2017,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.834
and he personally signed checks

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.602
for payments to Michael Cohen

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.637
for each of these nine months.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:46.873
In total

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.341
The grand jury found

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.076
there were 34 documents

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.112
with this critical false statement.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.915
Why did Donald Trump

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.718
repeatedly make these false statements?

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.753
The evidence will show that he did so

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.921
to cover up

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.958
crimes relating to the 2016 election

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.761
Donald Trump executives at the publishing

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.030
company American Media Inc.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:12.298
Mr.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:16.069
Cohen and others agreed in 2015

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.872
to a catch and kill scheme.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:22.442
That is a scheme to buy and suppress

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.578
negative information to help Mr.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.413
Trump's chance of winning the election.

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.550
As part of this scheme.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.784
Donald Trump and others

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.453
made three payments

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:33.953
to people

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.089
who claim to have negative information

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.991
about Mr. Trump

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.326
to make these payments.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.595
They set up shell companies

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.863
and they made yet more

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.231
false statements,

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.332
including, for example,

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.835
in AMI American Media Inc's

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.436
business records,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.473
one of the three people who they paid

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.274
to keep quiet

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.510
was a woman named Stormy Daniels

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.678
less than two weeks

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.480
before the presidential election.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.915
Michael Cohen

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:05.351
wired $130,000 to Stormy Daniels lawyer.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.487
That payment

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.489
was the high, damaging information

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.958
from the voting public

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.828
The participants scheme was illegal.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.197
The scheme violated New York

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.498
election law,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.767
which makes it a crime to conspire

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.803
to promote a candidacy by a lawful means.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.373
The $130,000 wire payment

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.274
exceeded

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.376
the federal campaign contribution cap,

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.746
and the false statements in its books

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.782
violated New York law.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.852
That is why Mr.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.788
Trump made false statements

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:44.190
about his payments to Mr. Cohen.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.292
He could not simply say

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.628
that the payments were a reimbursement

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:48.995
for Mr.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.797
Cohen's payments

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.666
to Sandy to Stormy Daniels.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.467
To do so.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:54.867
To make

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.135
that true statement

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.338
would have been to omit a crime.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.573
